  {
    "## Limitations & Future Work\n",
    "\n",
    "- Single ticker (IBM or synthetic) — results shouldn't be generalized to \"which architecture is\n",
    "  best for time series\" without testing on multiple, structurally different series.\n",
    "- No exogenous features (volume, macro indicators, sentiment) — purely univariate.\n",
    "- No probabilistic/uncertainty output (point forecasts only); quantile or conformal prediction\n",
    "  intervals would be a natural next step, especially for a task where uncertainty is decision-relevant.\n",
    "- Hyperparameters (hidden size, learning rate, NSTEPS) were fixed rather than tuned per model,\n",
    "  to keep the comparison fair and the study tractable — a proper study would tune each\n",
    "  architecture's own hyperparameters via nested walk-forward CV.\n"
